@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix bibo:    <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/> .
@prefix vann:    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .
@prefix prov:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix cc:      <http://creativecommons.org/ns#> .

@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix schema:  <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix arch:    <https://meta.linked.archi/core#> .
@prefix ad:      <https://meta.linked.archi/arch-decision#> .
@prefix :        <https://meta.linked.archi/arch-processes#> .

<https://meta.linked.archi/arch-processes#>
    rdf:type                      owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports                   arch: ;
    cc:license                    "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri    "https://meta.linked.archi/arch-processes#" ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "ap" ;
    dcterms:creator               "Kalin Maldzhanski"^^xsd:string ;
    dcterms:title                      "Linked.Archi Architecture Processes Extension"@en ;
    dcterms:description                '''Extension ontology describing architecture governance processes,
activities, tasks, and their inputs and outputs.

Architecture processes are not constituents of the system being architected —
they are the governance and lifecycle infrastructure that acts upon it from the
outside. An architecture review board process governs a system; it is not part
of the system's architecture. They are elements of a model all the same — of a
model of the architecture practice: a process, its activities, tasks,
deliverables and milestones are element types (arch:Element), so that a
modelling tool can place them in a view beside the architecture they govern.
Process concepts relate to the elements of that architecture via linking
properties (ap:governs, ap:input, ap:output, ap:consumedBy), never by being
one of its components.

Use this extension when you need to:
* Describe architecture governance processes and their decomposition
* Capture process inputs (forces, models, information items) and outputs
  (decisions, deliverables, models)
* Trace how architecture activities relate to decisions and deliverables
* Link architecture elements to the processes that govern them

The process concepts are aligned with ISO/IEC/IEEE 42020 (architecture governance),
ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207 (software lifecycle), and ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288 (system lifecycle).
For the normative standard definitions themselves, see the corresponding standard
vocabularies under standards/.'''@en ;
    dcterms:abstract              '''Ontology describing architecture governance processes, activities,
tasks, and their inputs/outputs — governance infrastructure that acts upon
architecture elements, not constituents of the architecture itself.'''@en ;
    dcterms:created               "2020-07-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:issued                "2020-07-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:modified              "2026-11-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dcterms:publisher                  <https://linked.archi>,
                                  "Linked.Archi"@en ;
    bibo:status                   "draft" ;
    owl:versionIRI                <https://meta.linked.archi/arch-processes/0.4.0#> ;
    owl:versionInfo               "0.4.0"@en ;
    owl:priorVersion              <https://meta.linked.archi/arch-processes/0.3.0#> ;
    schema:citation               "Linked.Archi Architecture Processes Extension" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom           "ISO/IEC/IEEE 42020:2019",
                                  "ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207:2017",
                                  "ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288:2023" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso                  <https://www.iso.org/standard/68982.html>,
                                  <https://www.iso.org/standard/63712.html>,
                                  <https://www.iso.org/standard/81702.html>,
                                  <https://iasa-global.github.io/btabok/architecture_lifecycle.html>,
                                  <http://dx.doi.org/10.1109/WICSA.2014.32>,
                                  <http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-87879-7_14>,
                                  <http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.jss.2015.08.054> ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Classes — Architecture Process Concepts
##
## These classes describe the governance and lifecycle infrastructure that
## acts upon architecture elements. They are NOT subclasses of arch:Element
## because they do not constitute the architecture — they govern it.
##
## Architecture elements relate to processes via linking properties:
##   ap:governs        — process governs an element
##   ap:input/output   — process consumes/produces elements
##   ap:consumedBy     — element is consumed by a process
##
## For the normative ISO standard definitions, see:
##   standards/iso42020/iso42020.ttl  — architecture governance processes
##   standards/iso12207/iso12207.ttl  — software lifecycle processes
##   standards/iso15288/iso15288.ttl  — system lifecycle processes
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:ArchitectureProcess
    a                owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf  arch:Element ;
    skos:prefLabel   "Architecture Process"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''A process within the architecture governance or lifecycle framework.
An architecture process transforms inputs (information items, models, forces)
into outputs (decisions, deliverables, models) through a structured set of
activities and tasks.

Processes can represent governance workflows (e.g., architecture review boards),
lifecycle phases (e.g., architecture elaboration), or operational procedures
(e.g., change impact assessment).

Architecture processes are not part of the architecture being described — they
are the governance infrastructure that acts upon it. An architecture review
board governs systems; it is not itself a system component. In a model it is an
element like any other: an element of a model of the practice, which a view may
show beside what the process governs.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote   '''Aligned with the process concept from ISO/IEC/IEEE 42020, 12207, and 15288.
Use ap:governs to link a process to the architecture elements it governs.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:ArchReviewProcess a ap:ArchitectureProcess ;
    skos:prefLabel "Architecture Review Board Process"@en ;
    ap:hasActivity ex:ReviewPreparation, ex:ReviewExecution, ex:ReviewFollowUp ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://meta.linked.archi/iso42020#ArchitectureGovernance> .'''@en ;
.

:ProcessActivity
    a                owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf  arch:Element ;
    skos:prefLabel   "Process Activity"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''A cohesive set of tasks within an architecture process that contributes
to achieving the process purpose. Activities decompose a process into
manageable units of work.

An activity groups related tasks and may have its own inputs and outputs.
Activities are ordered within a process and may have dependencies on
other activities.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote   '''Aligned with the activity concept from ISO/IEC/IEEE 42020, 12207, and 15288.
Activities provide the intermediate decomposition level between processes and tasks.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:StakeholderAnalysis a ap:ProcessActivity ;
    skos:prefLabel "Stakeholder Analysis"@en ;
    ap:activityOfProcess ex:ArchConceptualization ;
    ap:hasTask ex:IdentifyStakeholders, ex:PrioritizeConcerns .'''@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso42020#Activity>,
                     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso12207#Activity>,
                     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso15288#Activity> ;
.

:ProcessTask
    a                owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf  arch:Element ;
    skos:prefLabel   "Process Task"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''A specific action or work item within a process activity. Tasks are
the finest-grained units of work in the process decomposition.

A task is a requirement, recommendation, or permissible action intended
to contribute to the achievement of one or more outcomes of a process.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote   '''Aligned with the task concept from ISO/IEC/IEEE 42020, 12207, and 15288.
Tasks are the leaf-level work items that can be assigned, tracked, and verified.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:IdentifyStakeholders a ap:ProcessTask ;
    skos:prefLabel "Identify stakeholders and their concerns"@en ;
    ap:taskOfActivity ex:StakeholderAnalysis ;
    ap:performedBy ex:SolutionArchitect .'''@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso42020#Task>,
                     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso12207#Task>,
                     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso15288#Task> ;
.

:ProcessDeliverable
    a                owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf  arch:Element ;
    skos:prefLabel   "Process Deliverable"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''A required output of a process that must be formally delivered to a
stakeholder. Deliverables are the tangible work products that result
from process execution — documents, models, assessments, or other
artifacts.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote   '''Aligned with the deliverable concept from ISO/IEC/IEEE 42020, 12207, and 15288.
Deliverables bridge the process world and the architecture description world —
a deliverable may be an architecture model, a decision record, or a governance report.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:ArchDefinitionDoc a ap:ProcessDeliverable ;
    skos:prefLabel "Architecture Definition Document"@en ;
    ap:producedBy ex:ArchElaborationProcess .'''@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso42020#Deliverable>,
                     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso12207#Deliverable>,
                     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso15288#Deliverable> ;
.

:InformationItem
    a                owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf  :ProcessDeliverable ;
    skos:prefLabel   "Information Item"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''A separately identifiable body of information that is produced, stored,
and delivered for human use. Information items are the currency of
process communication — they flow between processes as inputs and outputs.'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote   '''Aligned with the information item concept from ISO/IEC/IEEE 42020, 12207, and 15288.
An information item is a more general concept than a deliverable — not all information
items are formal deliverables, but all deliverables contain information items.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:ArchProposal a ap:InformationItem ;
    skos:prefLabel "Architecture Proposal Document"@en ;
    skos:definition "The solution architect proposal including context, options, and rationale."@en ;
    ap:consumedBy ex:ArchReviewProcess .'''@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso42020#InformationItem>,
                     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso12207#InformationItem>,
                     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso15288#InformationItem> ;
.

:ProcessMilestone
    a                owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf  arch:Element ;
    skos:prefLabel   "Process Milestone"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''A significant point or event in a process that marks the completion
of a set of activities or the achievement of a key objective.
Milestones are used for governance checkpoints, phase gates,
and progress tracking.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:ArchReviewGate a ap:ProcessMilestone ;
    skos:prefLabel "Architecture Review Gate"@en ;
    ap:milestoneOfProcess ex:ArchGovernanceProcess .'''@en ;
.

:ProcessRole
    a                owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf  arch:Stakeholder ;
    skos:prefLabel   "Process Role"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''A role that a stakeholder plays within an architecture process.
Process roles define responsibilities and authorities for process
execution — who performs, reviews, approves, or is informed about
process activities.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:ChiefArchitect a ap:ProcessRole ;
    skos:prefLabel "Chief Architect"@en ;
    ap:responsibleFor ex:ArchGovernanceProcess .'''@en ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Properties — Process Structure
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:hasActivity
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "has activity"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links an ArchitectureProcess to a ProcessActivity that is part of it.
Activities decompose a process into manageable units of work.'''@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ArchitectureProcess ;
    rdfs:range       :ProcessActivity ;
.

:activityOfProcess
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf    :hasActivity ;
    skos:prefLabel   "activity of process"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a ProcessActivity to the ArchitectureProcess it belongs to."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ProcessActivity ;
    rdfs:range       :ArchitectureProcess ;
.

:hasTask
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "has task"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a ProcessActivity to a ProcessTask that is part of it."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ProcessActivity ;
    rdfs:range       :ProcessTask ;
.

:taskOfActivity
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf    :hasTask ;
    skos:prefLabel   "task of activity"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a ProcessTask to the ProcessActivity it belongs to."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ProcessTask ;
    rdfs:range       :ProcessActivity ;
.

:hasSubProcess
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "has sub-process"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links an ArchitectureProcess to a child ArchitectureProcess,
enabling hierarchical process decomposition.'''@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ArchitectureProcess ;
    rdfs:range       :ArchitectureProcess ;
.

:milestoneOfProcess
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "milestone of process"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a ProcessMilestone to the ArchitectureProcess it belongs to."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ProcessMilestone ;
    rdfs:range       :ArchitectureProcess ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Properties — Governance Links
##
## These properties bridge the process layer to the architecture layer.
## Architecture elements are linked TO processes — processes are not
## themselves architecture elements.
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:governs
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "governs"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links an ArchitectureProcess to the architecture element(s) it
governs. The governed elements are constituents of the architecture;
the process is the governance infrastructure that acts upon them.'''@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ArchitectureProcess ;
    rdfs:range       arch:Element ;
.

:governedBy
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf    :governs ;
    skos:prefLabel   "governed by"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links an architecture element to the ArchitectureProcess that
governs it.'''@en ;
    rdfs:domain      arch:Element ;
    rdfs:range       :ArchitectureProcess ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Properties — Process Inputs and Outputs
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:input
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "input"@en ;
    skos:definition      '''An information item, model, or artifact consumed by a process.
Inputs can include architecture models, metamodels, forces (requirements,
constraints), information items, or any other element that feeds into
the process.'''@en ;
    rdfs:domain          :ArchitectureProcess ;
    schema:rangeIncludes :InformationItem,
                         arch:Metamodel,
                         arch:Model,
                         ad:Force ;
.

:output
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "output"@en ;
    skos:definition      '''An information item, model, or artifact produced by a process.
Outputs can include architecture models, decisions, deliverables,
information items, or any other element that results from process
execution.'''@en ;
    rdfs:domain          :ArchitectureProcess ;
    schema:rangeIncludes :InformationItem,
                         :ProcessDeliverable,
                         arch:Metamodel,
                         arch:Model,
                         ad:Decision ;
.

:producedBy
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf    :output ;
    skos:prefLabel   "produced by"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a ProcessDeliverable to the ArchitectureProcess that produces it."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ProcessDeliverable ;
    rdfs:range       :ArchitectureProcess ;
.

:consumedBy
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf    :input ;
    skos:prefLabel   "consumed by"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links an element to the ArchitectureProcess that consumes it as input."@en ;
    rdfs:range       :ArchitectureProcess ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Properties — Process Roles and Responsibilities
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:responsibleFor
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "responsible for"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links a ProcessRole (or Stakeholder) to the ArchitectureProcess
they are responsible for executing or governing.'''@en ;
    rdfs:domain      arch:Stakeholder ;
    rdfs:range       :ArchitectureProcess ;
.

:performedBy
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "performed by"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a ProcessActivity or ProcessTask to the role that performs it."@en ;
    rdfs:range       :ProcessRole ;
.

:approvedBy
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "approved by"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a ProcessDeliverable or ProcessMilestone to the role that approves it."@en ;
    rdfs:range       :ProcessRole ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Properties — Process Dependencies and Sequencing
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:precedes
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "precedes"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links a process element to another that must follow it.
Used for sequencing activities, tasks, or milestones within a process.'''@en ;
    owl:inverseOf    :follows ;
.

:follows
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "follows"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links a process element to another that must precede it.
Used for sequencing activities, tasks, or milestones within a process.'''@en ;
    owl:inverseOf    :precedes ;
.

:triggeredBy
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "triggered by"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links a process to the event or condition that triggers its execution.
The trigger can be a milestone, a decision, an external event, or
a change in the architecture.'''@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ArchitectureProcess ;
.

:relatedProcess
    a                owl:ObjectProperty, owl:SymmetricProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "related process"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links an ArchitectureProcess to another related process."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :ArchitectureProcess ;
    rdfs:range       :ArchitectureProcess ;
.



## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Classes — Lifecycle Stage Concepts
##
## A lifecycle stage is a distinct phase in the lifecycle of a system,
## software product, service, or portfolio item. Lifecycle stages are
## complementary to processes — a process may be associated with one or
## more lifecycle stages, but stages themselves represent states/phases,
## not activities.
##
## Domain ontologies (TIME, Tech Radar, etc.) define their own lifecycle
## enumerations as subclasses or instances of LifecycleStage.
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:LifecycleStage
    a                owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf  skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel   "Lifecycle Stage"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''A distinct phase in the lifecycle of a system, software product,
service, or portfolio item. Lifecycle stages represent states that an
entity passes through over time — from initial conception through active
use to eventual retirement.

Lifecycle stages are not processes — they are the phases within which
processes execute. A stage answers "where is it now?" while a process
answers "what happens during that phase?"'''@en ;
    skos:scopeNote   '''Aligned with lifecycle concepts from:
* ISO/IEC/IEEE 12207:2017 (software lifecycle stages)
* ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288:2023 (system lifecycle stages)
* SAP LeanIX (application lifecycle: Plan, Phase In, Active, Phase Out, End of Life)

This extension defines a canonical, notation-agnostic stage set as instances of
this class: :Plan, :PhaseIn, :Active, :PhaseOut, :Retired, grouped by
:ApplicationLifecycle. Use those unless a domain genuinely needs its own.

Domain ontologies may define their own stage sets as subclasses or instances:
* timefw:LifecycleState (Plan, Build, Run, Retire)
* radar:Ring (Adopt, Trial, Assess, Hold) — analogous to technology lifecycle
* iso12207 stage individuals (Concept, Development, Production, Utilization,
  Support, Retirement)'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:ActiveStage a ap:LifecycleStage ;
    skos:prefLabel "Active"@en ;
    ap:partOfLifecycle ex:ApplicationLifecycle ;
    ap:stageOrder 3 .'''@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso12207#>,
                     <https://meta.linked.archi/iso15288#> ;
.

:LifecycleModel
    a                owl:Class ;
    skos:prefLabel   "Lifecycle Model"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''A named collection of lifecycle stages defining a complete lifecycle
progression for a category of entities. Different domains use different
lifecycle models — software products, enterprise applications, technology
components, and services each have distinct stage sets.

A lifecycle model defines the valid stages and their ordering. Individual
entities are associated with a single stage at any point in time.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:ApplicationLifecycle a ap:LifecycleModel ;
    skos:prefLabel "Application Portfolio Lifecycle"@en ;
    ap:hasStage ex:Plan, ex:Build, ex:Run, ex:Retire .'''@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso     <https://www.iso.org/standard/63712.html>,
                     <https://www.iso.org/standard/81702.html> ;
.


## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Properties — Lifecycle Structure
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:atLifecycleStage
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "at lifecycle stage"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links a resource to the lifecycle stage it currently occupies.
Applicable to architecture elements (applications, systems, services)
and to architecture models (to indicate elaboration maturity).
Domain ontologies may define more specific sub-properties
(e.g., timefw:lifecycleState) for their own contexts.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''# Application lifecycle
ex:PaymentPlatform a am:ApplicationComponent ;
    ap:atLifecycleStage timefw:Run ;
    ap:followsLifecycle ex:ApplicationLifecycle .

# Architecture work maturity (ISO 42020 phases)
ex:PaymentArchDescription a arch:Model ;
    ap:atLifecycleStage ex:Elaboration .'''@en ;
    rdfs:range       :LifecycleStage ;
.

:followsLifecycle
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "follows lifecycle"@en ;
    skos:definition  '''Links a resource to the lifecycle model that governs its
progression through stages. Applicable to architecture elements
and to architecture models.'''@en ;
    skos:example     '''ex:PaymentPlatform ap:followsLifecycle ex:ApplicationLifecycle .
ex:ApplicationLifecycle a ap:LifecycleModel ;
    skos:prefLabel "Application Portfolio Lifecycle"@en ;
    ap:hasStage timefw:Plan, timefw:Build, timefw:Run, timefw:Retire .'''@en ;
    rdfs:range       :LifecycleModel ;
.

:partOfLifecycle
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "part of lifecycle"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a LifecycleStage to the LifecycleModel it belongs to."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :LifecycleStage ;
    rdfs:range       :LifecycleModel ;
.

:hasStage
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf    :partOfLifecycle ;
    skos:prefLabel   "has stage"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a LifecycleModel to a LifecycleStage that is part of it."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :LifecycleModel ;
    rdfs:range       :LifecycleStage ;
.

:stageOrder
    a                owl:DatatypeProperty, owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "stage order"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Numeric ordering of a lifecycle stage within its lifecycle model (1-based)."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :LifecycleStage ;
    rdfs:range       xsd:integer ;
.

:nextStage
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel   "next stage"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a LifecycleStage to the stage that typically follows it in the lifecycle progression."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :LifecycleStage ;
    rdfs:range       :LifecycleStage ;
.

:previousStage
    a                owl:ObjectProperty ;
    owl:inverseOf    :nextStage ;
    skos:prefLabel   "previous stage"@en ;
    skos:definition  "Links a LifecycleStage to the stage that typically precedes it in the lifecycle progression."@en ;
    rdfs:domain      :LifecycleStage ;
    rdfs:range       :LifecycleStage ;
.

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
## Individuals — Portfolio Lifecycle Stages
##
## The canonical, notation-agnostic stage set. Nothing about "Active" or
## "Phase Out" derives from ArchiMate, C4, or Backstage, so these stages live
## here rather than in any modeling language's assets — versioning them per
## notation release would attach a version axis with no source.
##
## Typed :LifecycleStage only. Because :LifecycleStage is rdfs:subClassOf
## skos:Concept, these are SKOS concepts by entailment; explicit skos:Concept
## typing would be redundant. They are deliberately not placed in a
## skos:ConceptScheme — per DD-23, a second home invites a competing copy.
##
## The five-stage progression follows the SAP LeanIX application lifecycle
## already cited in the scopeNote on :LifecycleStage. Mappings to ISO 12207 and
## the TIME framework are asserted in those files, which already import this
## one, so the dependency direction stays consistent.
##
## Note the distinction between :PhaseOut and :Retired, which ISO 12207 and the
## TIME framework both collapse into a single stage.
## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

:ApplicationLifecycle
    a                  :LifecycleModel ;
    skos:prefLabel     "Application Portfolio Lifecycle"@en ;
    skos:definition    '''Five-stage lifecycle progression for portfolio assets — applications,
technology components, and services alike.'''@en ;
    :hasStage          :Plan, :PhaseIn, :Active, :PhaseOut, :Retired ;
    dcterms:source     <https://docs-eam.leanix.net/docs/lifecycle> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso       <https://docs-eam.leanix.net/docs/lifecycle> ;
.

:Plan
    a                  :LifecycleStage ;
    skos:prefLabel     "Plan"@en ;
    skos:definition    "Asset is planned or proposed but not yet being built or acquired."@en ;
    :partOfLifecycle   :ApplicationLifecycle ;
    :stageOrder        1 ;
    :nextStage         :PhaseIn ;
    skos:closeMatch    <https://docs-eam.leanix.net/docs/lifecycle#plan> ;
.

:PhaseIn
    a                  :LifecycleStage ;
    skos:prefLabel     "Phase In"@en ;
    skos:altLabel      "Build"@en ;
    skos:definition    '''Asset is being developed, acquired, or rolled out, and is not yet in
full operational use.'''@en ;
    :partOfLifecycle   :ApplicationLifecycle ;
    :stageOrder        2 ;
    :nextStage         :Active ;
    skos:closeMatch    <https://docs-eam.leanix.net/docs/lifecycle#phase-in> ;
.

:Active
    a                  :LifecycleStage ;
    skos:prefLabel     "Active"@en ;
    skos:altLabel      "Run"@en ;
    skos:definition    "Asset is in active operational use, providing its intended services."@en ;
    :partOfLifecycle   :ApplicationLifecycle ;
    :stageOrder        3 ;
    :nextStage         :PhaseOut ;
    skos:closeMatch    <https://docs-eam.leanix.net/docs/lifecycle#active> ;
.

:PhaseOut
    a                  :LifecycleStage ;
    skos:prefLabel     "Phase Out"@en ;
    skos:definition    '''Asset is being decommissioned — still operational for some consumers,
but closed to new use and scheduled for withdrawal.'''@en ;
    :partOfLifecycle   :ApplicationLifecycle ;
    :stageOrder        4 ;
    :nextStage         :Retired ;
    skos:closeMatch    <https://docs-eam.leanix.net/docs/lifecycle#phase-out> ;
    skos:scopeNote     '''Distinct from :Retired. An asset in phase-out still runs; an asset that
is retired does not.'''@en ;
.

:Retired
    a                  :LifecycleStage ;
    skos:prefLabel     "Retired"@en ;
    skos:altLabel      "End of Life"@en ;
    skos:definition    '''Asset has been withdrawn from service. Data is archived or migrated and
resources are reclaimed.'''@en ;
    :partOfLifecycle   :ApplicationLifecycle ;
    :stageOrder        5 ;
    skos:closeMatch    <https://docs-eam.leanix.net/docs/lifecycle#end-of-life> ;
.

#################################################################
# Relationship types — the links that are drawn
#
# For each link whose two ends can be placed on a view, a qualified
# relationship class whose unqualified form is the predicate above, with
# its qualified property: a tool that draws one writes the same triple a
# tool that sets the property writes, with a relationship resource beside
# it. The class is named after its predicate.
#################################################################

:HasActivity
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :hasActivity ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Has Activity"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from an Architecture Process to a Process Activity it is made of."@en ;
.

:qualifiedHasActivity
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified has Activity"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Has Activity link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :HasActivity ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :hasActivity ;
.

:HasTask
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :hasTask ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Has Task"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from a Process Activity to a Process Task it is made of."@en ;
.

:qualifiedHasTask
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified has Task"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Has Task link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :HasTask ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :hasTask ;
.

:HasSubProcess
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :hasSubProcess ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Has Sub-Process"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from an Architecture Process to a child Architecture Process."@en ;
.

:qualifiedHasSubProcess
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified has Sub-Process"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Has Sub-Process link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :HasSubProcess ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :hasSubProcess ;
.

:MilestoneOfProcess
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :milestoneOfProcess ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Milestone Of"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from a Process Milestone to the Architecture Process it belongs to."@en ;
.

:qualifiedMilestoneOfProcess
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified milestone Of"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Milestone Of link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :MilestoneOfProcess ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :milestoneOfProcess ;
.

:Precedes
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :precedes ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Precedes"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from a process, activity, task or milestone to the one that must follow it."@en ;
.

:qualifiedPrecedes
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified precedes"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Precedes link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :Precedes ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :precedes ;
.

:Input
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :input ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Input"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from an Architecture Process to an information item or a force it consumes."@en ;
.

:qualifiedInput
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified input"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Input link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :Input ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :input ;
.

:Output
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :output ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Output"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from an Architecture Process to a deliverable, an information item or a decision it produces."@en ;
.

:qualifiedOutput
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified output"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Output link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :Output ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :output ;
.

:PerformedBy
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :performedBy ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Performed By"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from a Process Activity or Process Task to the role that performs it."@en ;
.

:qualifiedPerformedBy
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified performed By"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Performed By link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :PerformedBy ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :performedBy ;
.

:ApprovedBy
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :approvedBy ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Approved By"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from a Process Deliverable or Process Milestone to the role that approves it."@en ;
.

:qualifiedApprovedBy
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified approved By"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Approved By link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :ApprovedBy ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :approvedBy ;
.

:Governs
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :governs ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Governs"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from an Architecture Process to an architecture element it governs."@en ;
.

:qualifiedGoverns
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified governs"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Governs link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :Governs ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :governs ;
.

:ResponsibleFor
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :responsibleFor ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Responsible For"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from a Process Role or Stakeholder to the Architecture Process they are responsible for executing or governing."@en ;
.

:qualifiedResponsibleFor
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified responsible For"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Responsible For link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :ResponsibleFor ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :responsibleFor ;
.

:RelatedProcess
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :relatedProcess ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Related Process"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link between two Architecture Processes related to each other."@en ;
.

:qualifiedRelatedProcess
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified related Process"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Related Process link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :RelatedProcess ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :relatedProcess ;
.

:TriggeredBy
    a                    owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf      arch:QualifiedRelationship ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :triggeredBy ;
    skos:prefLabel       "Triggered By"@en ;
    skos:definition      "A drawn link from an Architecture Process to the event or condition that triggers it: a milestone, a decision, an event or a change in the architecture."@en ;
.

:qualifiedTriggeredBy
    a                    owl:ObjectProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel       "qualified triggered By"@en ;
    skos:definition      "Links the source of a drawn Triggered By link to its relationship resource."@en ;
    rdfs:range           :TriggeredBy ;
    arch:unqualifiedForm :triggeredBy ;
.

#################################################################
# Typical ends of the predicates drawn
#
# Modelling-tool guidance (arch:domainIncludes, arch:rangeIncludes): where
# a line of each kind usually starts and ends. An end that is no element —
# a model, a metamodel, a quality attribute, a pattern — is not drawn, and
# is not listed.
#################################################################

:hasActivity
    arch:domainIncludes  :ArchitectureProcess ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ProcessActivity ;
.

:hasTask
    arch:domainIncludes  :ProcessActivity ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ProcessTask ;
.

:hasSubProcess
    arch:domainIncludes  :ArchitectureProcess ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ArchitectureProcess ;
.

:milestoneOfProcess
    arch:domainIncludes  :ProcessMilestone ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ArchitectureProcess ;
.

:precedes
    arch:domainIncludes  :ArchitectureProcess, :ProcessActivity, :ProcessTask, :ProcessMilestone ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ArchitectureProcess, :ProcessActivity, :ProcessTask, :ProcessMilestone ;
.

:input
    arch:domainIncludes  :ArchitectureProcess ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :InformationItem, ad:Force ;
.

:output
    arch:domainIncludes  :ArchitectureProcess ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ProcessDeliverable, ad:Decision ;
.

:performedBy
    arch:domainIncludes  :ProcessActivity, :ProcessTask ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ProcessRole ;
.

:approvedBy
    arch:domainIncludes  :ProcessDeliverable, :ProcessMilestone ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ProcessRole ;
.

:governs
    arch:domainIncludes  :ArchitectureProcess ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   arch:Element ;
.

:responsibleFor
    arch:domainIncludes  :ProcessRole, arch:Stakeholder ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ArchitectureProcess ;
.

:relatedProcess
    arch:domainIncludes  :ArchitectureProcess ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ArchitectureProcess ;
.

:triggeredBy
    arch:domainIncludes  :ArchitectureProcess ;
    arch:rangeIncludes   :ProcessMilestone, ad:Decision, arch:Element ;
.
